<% content_for :title, "Data processing terms" %>
<% content_for :description, "How HardPoint processes the personal data your hardware store keeps about customers, staff and suppliers, as your processor under Kenya's Data Protection Act, 2019." %>
<%# The data processing agreement every shop accepts at signup. Written to match what the app does; a lawyer should review it before launch. %>

<div class="lp">
<article>
  <%= render "pages/page_head", kicker: "The fine print", title: "Data processing terms", center: false do %>
    <p class="lp-lede">Part of the <%= link_to "terms of service", terms_path, class: "link" %>. Your shop is the data controller for the personal data it keeps in HardPoint; <%= @company[:name] %> processes it on your instructions, as your data processor under the Data Protection Act, 2019. Last changed <%= l(Date.new(2026, 11, 8), format: :long) %>.</p>
  <% end %>

  <div class="lp-wrap pb-[96px]">
  <div class="lp-doc max-w-[760px]">

  <% [
    [ "What personal data is processed", "Customers: names, phone numbers, email addresses, KRA PINs, addresses, what they bought and what they owe. Suppliers: contact names, phone numbers and email addresses. Your staff: names, email addresses, roles, sign-ins and what they did in HardPoint. People who pay by M-Pesa or Airtel Money: the name and number the payment came from. Visitors to your online store: the name, number and email they type when ordering." ],
    [ "Why, and on whose instructions", "Only to provide HardPoint to your shop: ringing up sales, keeping accounts, sending receipts and statements you ask it to send, signing sales with KRA, matching payments, and showing your staff what they're allowed to see. Your instructions are what you and your staff do in HardPoint and these terms. We don't use the data for anything else, don't sell it, and don't combine it across shops." ],
    [ "Who at HardPoint can see it", "Only platform staff who need to, to support you or keep the service running, and each time someone signs in to your shop to help you it's recorded in your shop's Activity, visible to you. Platform staff sign in with two-factor codes." ],
    [ "Where it's kept", "On servers with #{Rails.application.credentials.dig(:hosting, :provider) || "Contabo (Germany)"} behind Cloudflare, and in encrypted backups in a separate data centre. Where data leaves Kenya it does so with the safeguards the Act requires: it stays encrypted in transit and in backups, under contracts with providers that protect it to at least the Act's standard." ],
    [ "Other processors we use", "Cloudflare (traffic and protection), Amazon Web Services (email), Safaricom (M-Pesa), Airtel Africa (Airtel Money), the Kenya Revenue Authority (eTIMS), Paystack (card payments to HardPoint), Africa's Talking (text messages) and, if we use one, an error-reporting service that receives technical details of faults but not your shop's records. Each receives only what its job needs. We tell owners by email before adding a processor that would handle your shop's data." ],
    [ "How it's protected", "Each shop's data is kept apart from every other shop's inside the database itself. Connections are encrypted. Passwords are stored as one-way hashes; API keys, M-Pesa and eTIMS credentials and two-factor secrets are encrypted at rest; backups are encrypted before they leave the server. Phone numbers, PINs and payers' names are kept out of our logs. The controls are described in full in our security documentation, and the service is tested by an independent security firm." ],
    [ "Helping you with people's rights", "Your customers and staff can ask you to see, correct or delete what you hold about them. You can do all of that in HardPoint yourself: edit or remove a customer or supplier, remove a member of staff, or export everything. Sales records stay, because tax law requires them. If someone asks us directly, we send them to you and help you answer within the Act's time limits." ],
    [ "If something goes wrong", "If we learn of a breach affecting your shop's personal data, we tell your shop's owners without undue delay, and within 72 hours of learning of it, with what we know, what we're doing and what you should do, and we notify the Data Commissioner where the Act requires it." ],
    [ "How long we keep it", "For as long as your shop uses HardPoint. When you close the shop we delete its data 30 days later, and it leaves our backups within a further 35 days. We keep the invoices HardPoint issued to your shop, as tax law requires." ],
    [ "Your responsibilities as controller", "Tell your customers how you use their details, collect only what you need, keep your staff's access to what their role needs, and sign out devices you stop using. Register with the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner if your business is required to; HardPoint is registered as a processor." ],
    [ "Checking up on us", "Once a year, or after an incident, you can ask us for a summary of our security controls and the latest independent test, and we'll answer reasonable questions about how your data is processed." ],
    [ "Contact", "Data protection questions and requests: #{Rails.configuration.x.support[:email]}. Security reports: #{Rails.configuration.x.security_email}." ]
  ].each do |heading, body| %>
    <h2><%= heading %></h2>
    <p><%= body %></p>
  <% end %>
  </div>
  </div>
</article>
</div>
